# Techwave Delivery Intelligence -- frontend env
#
# MVP scope is one project / one sprint (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §11), and
# there is no `GET /projects` or `POST /projects` endpoint in the current
# API surface (§5.6) -- the Project row is created out-of-band (currently:
# by whatever seeds/ingests the backend DB; SCRUM-8's demo loader will own
# this). Until that seam exists, the frontend is pointed at the seeded
# project/sprint via env vars rather than discovering them at runtime.
VITE_PROJECT_ID=1
VITE_SPRINT_ID=3

# Static provenance label for the persistent "Demo data" indicator
# (ux-spec §3 "Universal state model", state 5 "Stale/demo").
# KNOWN GAP: SprintHealth/RiskFinding (backend/app/risk/schemas.py) do not
# yet surface Signal.provenance ("demo" | "live", see ARCHITECTURE.md §5.1)
# on these response contracts, so the frontend cannot read this from the
# API today. This env var is a placeholder until that field is added
# (flagged for architect/developer) -- do not treat it as backend truth.
VITE_DATA_PROVENANCE=demo

# Optional: override the backend origin the Vite dev proxy forwards
# /api/* to (see vite.config.ts). Defaults to http://localhost:8000.
# VITE_BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000
